  "worked_solution": "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{21} & =2\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =-2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
